From 666fb69f972ee43af58f8984ff62dfee0d691ef1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:39:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] key: add CKM_TPM2_ACTIVATE_CREDENTIAL, to chain an
 attestation key to the EK

An attestation key proves "the same TPM as before"; chaining it to the
TPM's Endorsement Key certificate proves "a genuine TPM". The client makes
a credential with TPM2_MakeCredential, for the EK public key and the
attestation key's Name, and only a TPM that holds both recovers it.

CKA_TPM2_EK_PUB_BLOB, on the private key of an attestation key, is the
public area of the default RSA 2048 EK of the TCG EK Credential Profile
(byte for byte what tpm2_createek makes), kept when the key is made.
CKA_TPM2_EK_CERT is the certificate the TPM holds for it in NV index
0x01C00002, read then with the owner's or the index's empty auth. Both
are absent if unavailable (an endorsement hierarchy with an auth value, no
certificate). They identify the TPM for good: only the user reads them
(CKR_ATTRIBUTE_SENSITIVE without the login, whatever handle the caller
holds), and an attestation key must be a private object.

CKM_TPM2_ACTIVATE_CREDENTIAL, for C_DecryptInit/C_Decrypt on that key,
takes the marshaled TPM2B_ID_OBJECT and TPM2B_ENCRYPTED_SECRET and returns
the credential. The EK is not an object of the token (a primary of the
endorsement hierarchy, not a child of the token's): the module makes it
for the operation, authorizes it with PolicySecret(endorsement), and flushes
it. A credential that does not parse or that the TPM refuses is
CKR_ENCRYPTED_DATA_INVALID. The operation ends with its one call, error
or not, except for a buffer too small.

Test: pkcs-activate-credential.int makes credentials with
TPM2_MakeCredential and recovers them, compares the EK with tpm2_createek's
and the certificate with the NV index's, checks that neither is readable
without the login, and checks the refusals and the sizes.
docs/VENDOR.md describes the interface and what the client verifies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
